DUNCAN CONTRACT INGEST / ROUTE CORRECTION — 2026-08-31

OWNER supplied `ZORR_REFERENCE_TO_DRAWING_ENGINE_MATH.md` as the governing math contract for the reference-drawing engine.

SOURCE FILE SHA256 = `a5926ba1f169d74a5562bd158ab6dc769090467aa7a1146541bd8a565bcac3c8`
SOURCE LINES = 734

## CORRECTION TO #228 INITIAL ROUTE
The initial #228 body made ComfyUI/IP-Adapter/ControlNet look like the primary engine route. That is too late in the pipeline.

The new contract establishes the hard base as:
`REFERENCE PIXELS -> EVIDENCE -> GEOMETRY -> TOPOLOGY -> PROPORTIONS -> TONE/COLOR MASSES -> STYLE TRANSFORMATION -> DRAWING -> PIXEL/STRUCTURE QC`

Therefore:
- deterministic reference analysis / structure state is PRIMARY;
- generative img2img / ControlNet / IP-Adapter is OPTIONAL DOWNSTREAM only;
- prompt prose is never geometry authority;
- no hidden anatomy/costume/props/background may be inferred as fact;
- each element must remain `OBSERVED | DERIVED | STYLE_TRANSFORM | UNKNOWN`;
- `UNKNOWN` geometry remains unresolved;
- no global magic PASS score or universal Canny/contour/style threshold is authorized.

## REUSE CHECK
Fresh Shared HQ code search found no existing implementation hits for `opencv`, `findContours`, `Sobel/Scharr/Canny`, or `silhouette_error_px`.

Upstream basis from the OWNER contract is verified:
- `opencv/opencv` exact ref `2ea6598f64f6f03d9d08db084a60585b0fc585f1` exists; repo license Apache-2.0.
- OpenCV upstream Canny at that ref already contains Sobel derivatives, magnitude, non-max suppression, double thresholding and hysteresis; ZORR must not reimplement that stack.
- upstream contour implementation exists at the same ref; use native contour topology/approximation primitives before any custom vectorizer.
- `google-ai-edge/mediapipe` exact ref `251c0cb9687230682929a64d413751f1a4f8a6d5` exists; repo license Apache-2.0. It remains OPTIONAL MEASUREMENT ONLY and may never authorize hidden anatomy.

## NEW CRITICAL PATH
`SOURCE INGEST`
`-> L0-L10 EVIDENCE DECOMPOSITION`
`-> VISIBLE SILHOUETTE + RAW/SIMPLIFIED CONTOURS`
`-> VISIBLE ANCHORS + PROPORTION GRAPH`
`-> OCCLUSION GRAPH + UNKNOWN MASK`
`-> COLOR/TONE/TEXTURE SUMMARIES`
`-> PROVENANCE PER ELEMENT`
`-> LOSS VECTOR E = [silhouette, anchor, proportion, occlusion, tone, color, texture, line_topology]`
`-> ONLY THEN STYLE RENDER / OPTIONAL GENERATIVE ASSIST`

## FIRST ACCEPTANCE SLICE
Before any renderer work, one reference analysis must emit at minimum:
- source width/height;
- visible bbox;
- visible silhouette;
- contours[] (raw + simplified + pixel error);
- anchors[] with original pixel coordinates and provenance;
- proportion graph;
- occlusion graph;
- color regions;
- tone summary;
- texture summary;
- uncertainty mask;
- provenance per element.

No image generation/editing is authorized by this contract ingest.

STATE = MATH CONTRACT INGESTED / PRIMARY ROUTE CORRECTED
COMFYUI = DOWNSTREAM OPTIONAL
CUSTOM CV ALGORITHM = FORBIDDEN UNTIL MEASURED OSS GAP
IMAGE GENERATION = NO
IMAGE EDITING = NO
NEXT = isolate the deterministic reference-analysis base using pinned OpenCV primitives; renderer remains blocked until the structure-state artifact exists.

